                  (f_{b})_{b}
                  \\big)_{b \colon B}
                  \\end{array}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToCoreaderAndState Relation to coreader- and state monad
          %p
            In a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,-] \colon \mathcal{C}\to \mathcal{C}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreader+comonad"} coreader comonad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\times (-)
          %p
            The composite of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreader+comonad"} coreader comonad
            followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+monad"} state monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,B \times (-)]
            This monad models the situation where a program may not only depend on a immutable parameter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \colon B
            but may be allowed to
            %em change
            it.
          %p
            Just as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreader+comonad"} coreader comonad
            canonically becomes a monad when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
          %h3#RelationToRandomVariables Relation to random variables in probability theory
          %p
            It makes sense to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,-]
            as producing spaces of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variables"} random variables
            (
            %a{:href => "#Verdier14"}> Verdier 14
            ) depending on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/possible+worlds"} possible worlds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#TorontoMcCarthy10b"}> Toronto &amp; McCarthy 10b, slide 24
            \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
            (While, from the perspective of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\ast \prod_W
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\ast \sum_W
            may be called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/necessity"} necessity
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/possibility"} possibility
          %blockquote
            %p
              The intuition behind the Reader monad, for a mathematician, is perhaps stochastic variables. A stochastic variable is a function from a probability space to some other space. So we see a stochastic variable as a monadic value. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Verdier14"}> Verdier 14
              \&amp;rbrack;
            %p
              you could interpret this by regarding random variables as reader monad computations. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#TorontoMcCarthy10b"}> Toronto &amp; McCarthy 10b, slide 35
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            %a{:href => "#TorontoMcCarthy10a"}> Toronto &amp; McCarthy 10a, 2.2
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Toronto14"} Toronto 14, 6.2
            call the function monad the
            = succeed "." do
              %em random variable idiom
          %p
            This is also brought out by the relation of
            %em linear
            reader algebras to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#QuantumReaderMonad"} below
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nondeterministic+computation"} nondeterministic computation
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "nondeterministic+computation#FormalizationViaIndefinitenessEffects"} Via indefiniteness effects
          %h3#FreeModules Free modules over the reader monad
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            for the
            = succeed "-reader" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/KleisliCatOfReaderMonad-221108.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
          %p
            (On the left we are showing the situation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+functor"} comparison functor
            and on the right we are using the
            %a{:href => "monad+in+computer+science#BasicIdea"} “bind”-notation
            from
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
          %h3#AlgebrasForTheReaderMonad General modules over the reader monad
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra
            of the reader monad on an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            consists of a single operation
